From 4eb5a0d7737762958a362ad6d4d42a8652f1da66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:35:31 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Gui: a translucent pixel counts in the stereo fit at the
 weighted mean of what it shows

The separation is the largest under which every pixel of the view stays
inside the person's depth limits, a translucent pixel's distance being the
mean of the layers it shows, each weighted by its share of the pixel's
colour.  Coin draws the transparent shapes after the opaque ones without
writing depth, so the measuring pass did not see a transparent shape
standing in front of everything else, and its pixels could pass the popped
limit.

The measuring pass is now drawn twice into a framebuffer with float colour,
with linear fog from the camera to beyond the far plane: toward white in the
first pass, toward black in the second, the background cleared to the
screen's distance in the first and to 0 in the second.  The fog is the viewer's own
SoEnvironment node's (Coin's linear HAZE), changed without notification for
the two passes and given back after them: that node is traversed after the
pass's callback, and with its fog (none by default) it would switch a fog
set with GL alone off again.  Every fragment's own
colour is the same in both, so the difference of the two pictures is, at
every pixel, the fog's share blended exactly as the layers are: the
contribution-weighted mean distance (as KiCad's patch 0006 of the edition
does with the fog over the distance).  A pixel drawn without the fog counts
at the depth of its surface.  Fog takes the distance without its sign,
so an orthographic volume that reaches behind the camera's plane is moved
along its axis for the fog, and its projection the other way (the picture
is the same).  The framebuffer's format is read back, since a driver may
give another than the one asked for.  Without a float framebuffer the transparent
shapes write depth in the one pass and count at their own distance, which
keeps every pixel inside the limits.  The trace says how many pixels were
translucent and unfogged.

Forwarded: not-needed (FreeCAD's AI_POLICY.md and AGENTS.md; the edition's build)
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic)
